wed the same ~18% error rate downstream of the worker. Mitigation: rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 (last healthy production release) in all regions; rollout verified. Follow-up: confirm worker and payments-api error rates recover, and root-cause v3.4.0 before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MHcWbnZB5QErVSqU2hqBDM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TYf5SfYev9rR7WqMb8LSfU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2 incident. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It reports healthy, and its error rate fell from 18% to 0.2%. v3.3.0 had been healthy in production before, so this didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, payments-worker) is open and on-call has been paged. It records the bad v3.4.0 deploy, the effect on payments-api, the rollback, and follow-ups: check that errors recover and find the root cause of v3.4.0 before redeploying it.\n\n**Still a problem:** payments-api is still unhealthy, at v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. It may just need time to catch up now that the worker is fixed. But its own history marks v5.1.0 as \"degraded,\" separate from the worker. So the API errors may not all be caused by the worker.\n\nI haven't changed payments-api, since you said the worker was the cause. I'd check its status again in a few minutes. If it's still failing, rolling it back to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release) is the next step. I can do that and add it to INC-0001 if you want.", "type": "text"}]}]}